{"className":"talk-topics","children":[["$","span","LLMs",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"LLMs"}],["$","span","Generative AI",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Generative AI"}],["$","span","GenAi",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"GenAi"}],["$","span","Embeddings",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Embeddings"}],["$","span","Optimization",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Optimization"}],["$","span","Synthetic Data",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Synthetic Data"}],["$","span","Workforce Planning",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Workforce Planning"}],["$","span","Python",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Python"}],["$","span","FastAPI",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"FastAPI"}],["$","span","Careers",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Careers"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","article","stream-java-linked-list-practice",{"className":"talk-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"talk-video","children":["$","iframe",null,{"src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/xSFrXbl_J6o","title":"Learning Java Together | Data Structures & Algorithms | Implementing Linked Lists in Java: Fundamentals and Traversal (Live Stream)","frameBorder":"0","allow":"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture","allowFullScreen":true,"className":"youtube-embed"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"talk-content","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"talk-title","children":"Learning Java Together | Data Structures & Algorithms | Implementing Linked Lists in Java: Fundamentals and Traversal (Live Stream)"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"talk-meta","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"talk-event","children":"Twitch Stream"}],["$","time",null,{"className":"talk-date","children":"February 29, 2024"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"talk-description","children":"This session focuses on building a singly linked list in Java from the ground up. Viewers are introduced to defining a `Node` class, constructing linked list elements, implementing the `appendToTail` method, and writing logic to traverse and print the list. The stream explores Java syntax, object-oriented design, and debugging techniques while relating key concepts to Python for context."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"talk-topics","children":[["$","span","Java",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Java"}],["$","span","Linked Lists",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Linked Lists"}],["$","span","Singly Linked List",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Singly Linked List"}],["$","span","Data Structures",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Data Structures"}],["$","span","Object-Oriented Programming",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Object-Oriented Programming"}],["$","span","Debugging",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Debugging"}],["$","span","Cracking the Coding Interview",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Cracking the Coding Interview"}],["$","span","Live Coding",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Live Coding"}],["$","span","Learning in Public",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Learning in Public"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","article","stream-java-linked-lists-and-cycle-detection",{"className":"talk-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"talk-video","children":["$","iframe",null,{"src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/AvcN5FrvNmk","title":"Learning Java Together | Data Structures & Algorithms | Linked Lists - Coding Practice |(Live Stream)","frameBorder":"0","allow":"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture","allowFullScreen":true,"className":"youtube-embed"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"talk-content","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"talk-title","children":"Learning Java Together | Data Structures & Algorithms | Linked Lists - Coding Practice |(Live Stream)"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"talk-meta","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"talk-event","children":"Twitch Stream"}],["$","time",null,{"className":"talk-date","children":"February 25, 2024"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"talk-description","children":"A deep dive into Java's linked list data structure and the Floyd's Cycle Detection algorithm using fast and slow pointers. A walk-through on how to build a linked list from scratch, exploring how nodes are appended, and debug-traces the creation of head-insertion logic. This stream transitions into a code walkthrough of detecting cycles in a linked list and reflects on debugging strategies, generic types, and practical Java syntax—all through hands-on experimentation and learning."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"talk-topics","children":[["$","span","Java",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Java"}],["$","span","Data Structures",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Data Structures"}],["$","span","Linked Lists",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Linked Lists"}],["$","span","Cycle Detection",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Cycle Detection"}],["$","span","Floyd's Algorithm",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Floyd's Algorithm"}],["$","span","Debugging",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Debugging"}],["$","span","Generics",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Generics"}],["$","span","Live Coding",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"Live Coding"}],["$","span","CS Fundamentals",{"className":"topic-tag","children":"CS Fundamentals"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","article","talk-building-a-rag-model",{"className":"talk-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"talk-video","children":["$","iframe",null,{"src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/tNJg1KJJrTk","title":"Building a RAG Model","frameBorder":"0","allow":"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture","allowFullScreen":true,"className":"youtube-embed"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"talk-content","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"talk-title","children":"Building a RAG Model"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"talk-meta","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"talk-event","children":"Twitch Stream"}],["$","tim